<title>USA: TWA cites short-term reduction in flying.</title>
<headline>TWA cites short-term reduction in flying.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc said Friday its March 1997 capacity and traffic declined from year-ago levels because of a planned short-term reduction in flying to make more aircraft available for scheduled maintenance and the planned downsizing of aircraft on some international routes.</p>
<p>Earlier, the carrier reported its March revenue passenger miles fell 4.4 percent from the same year-earlier period to 2.18 billion and available seat miles declined 7.6 percent to 2.99 billion miles.</p>
<p>TWA's stock ended up 4/16 at 6-7/16.</p>
<p>	  ((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
